      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا الْحَسَنِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنِ امْرَأَةٍ أَحَلَّتْ لِي جَارِيَتَهَا فَقَالَ ذَاكَ لَكَ قُلْتُ فَإِنْ كَانَتْ تَمْزَحُ قَالَ وَ كَيْفَ لَكَ بِمَا فِي قَلْبِهَا فَإِنْ عَلِمْتَ أَنَّهَا تَمْزَحُ فَلَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Muhammad Bin Ismail Bin Yzaie who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> about a woman who permitted her slave girl to me. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘That is for you’. I said, ‘Supposing it was in jest (as a joke)?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘And how could it be for you what is in her heart? So, if she were to let you know that rather it was in jest, so no’."
        ]
      }
    },
